WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.774 --> 00:00:04.060
FOR EACH OF THE NOMINEES FOR
BEST PRODUCTION DESIGN,

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.080
IT WAS A DREAM AND JOURNEY
THAT WASN'T ALWAYS CLEAR.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.000
GROWING UP, KATHY LUCAS LOVED
MOVIES BUT COULDN'T QUITE

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.460
FIGURE OUT WHERE SHE
FIT INTO MAKING THEM.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.140
AS A YOUNG ARCHITECTURE
STUDENT, NATHAN CROWLEY

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.679
HAD NO IDEA HE COULD EVER
BE A PART OF THE FILM INDUSTRY.

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:25.519
BUT TONIGHT, THEY ARE BOTH
NOMINATED FOR "TENET."

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:27.779
DONALD GRAHAM BURT SPENT THE
EARLY PART OF HIS CAREER

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:30.550
SWEEPING FLOORS AS
AN ON-SET JANITOR.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.891
JAN PASCALE WAS A 
PUPPET MASTER ON 

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:34.370
"MR. ROGER'S NEIGHBORHOOD."

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.792
WE RECOGNIZE THEIR INCREDIBLE
WORK TONIGHT ON "MANK."

00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:43.320
AND AS FATE WOULD HAVE IT, JAN
PASCALE WOULD LATER HIRE

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.414
MARK RICKER AS AN INTERN, WHICH
PUT HIM ON THE ROAD TO MAKING

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:51.819
 "MA RAINEY'S BLACK BOTTOM" ALONGSIDE
BRILLIANT SET DECORATORS

00:00:51.819 --> 00:00:54.548
DIANA STOUGHTON AND 
KAREN O'HARA.

00:00:54.548 --> 00:00:56.575
NOW, I WONDER, MARK

00:00:56.575 --> 00:01:00.750
WERE YOU THINKING ABOUT ANYTHING
WHEN YOU WERE GETTING JAN'S COFFEE?

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.800
I MEAN, LIKE, DID YOU
SEE THAT COMING?

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:04.960
JUST A THOUGHT.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.692
PETER FRANCIS TRAINED FOR MANY
YEARS AS A LANDSCAPE ARCHITECT.

00:01:08.692 --> 00:01:12.390
CATHY FEATHERSTONE COULDN'T STOP
THINKING ABOUT HOW TO CONSTRUCT

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:17.050
ONE-EYED WILLY'S SHIP AFTER
WATCHING "THE GOONIES" AS A KID,

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.330
SO SHE STARTED BUILDING SETS AND
DESIGNING COSTUMES FOR SCHOOL

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.670
PLAYS JUST BEFORE SHE TEAMED UP
WITH PETER ON "THE FATHER."

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:28.860
AND FINALLY, DAVID CRANK LANDED
IN MOTION PICTURE DESIGN

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.250
AFTER WORKING IN THEATER
FOR TEN YEARS.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.680
ELIZABETH KEENAN WORKED IN
ADVERTISING FOR 15 YEARS BEFORE

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.110
HOPPING ON A PLANE TO THE CZECH
REPUBLIC TO SECURE HER

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.450
FIRST SET DECORATING JOB.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.237
THEY ARE BOTH NOMINATED TONIGHT
FOR "NEWS OF THE WORLD."

00:01:49.037 --> 00:01:51.671
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:01:52.757 --> 00:01:54.183
"MANK"

00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:56.489
DONALD GRAHAM BURT,
PRODUCTION DESIGN

00:01:56.489 --> 00:01:58.823
AND JAN PASCALE,
SET DECORATION

00:01:58.823 --> 00:02:02.856
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:02:42.545 --> 00:02:46.190
IT’S A LONG WAY DOWN HERE.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:51.290
FIRST OF ALL, THANK YOU TO
DAVID FINCHER, CEÁN CHAFFIN

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.510
AND DON BURT FOR TRUSTING
ME WITH THIS AMAZING PROJECT.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:59.430
I’M JUST, IT WAS SUCH AN HONOR
TO WORK WITH SUCH AN

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.510
AMAZING GROUP OF PEOPLE.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.950
THANK YOU TO MY CREW WHO
WORKED THEIR TAILS OFF ON THIS,

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.250
JUST TO MAKE IT RIGHT.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.250
AND YOU KNOW, WHEN I WAS YOUNG,
I NEVER REALIZED THAT

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.990
THIS WAS A CAREER THAT WAS
EVEN A POSSIBILITY.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.770
THERE WERE SO MANY PEOPLE
THAT HELPED ME ALONG

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:21.470
THE WAY AND GUIDED ME
AND I’M SO GRATEFUL TO

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.850
ALL OF THEM AND ESPECIALLY
TO MY WIFE LOUISE,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.090
WHO INSPIRES ME EVERY DAY.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.700
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

